    "['peer [parameter1] label-route-capability check-tunnel-reachable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.3.1.1 send-label', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'address-family ipv4 unicast'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei BGP label-route-capability configuration:\\n\\n##\\nneighbor 10.3.1.1 send-label\\nneighbor 10.3.1.1 disable-connected-check\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. `send-label` is Cisco's equivalent to Huawei's `label-route-capability` for enabling MPLS label exchange in BGP\\n2. `disable-connected-check` serves a similar purpose to `check-tunnel-reachable` by allowing BGP sessions between non-directly connected peers when MPLS tunneling is used\\n\\nThe Cisco implementation doesn't have a direct 1:1 command for the tunnel reachability check, so we use these two commands to achieve similar functionality.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.3.1.1 send-label'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.3.1.1 disable-connected-check', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'address-family ipv4 unicast'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei BGP label-route-capability configuration:\\n\\n##\\nneighbor 10.3.1.1 send-label\\nneighbor 10.3.1.1 disable-connected-check\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. `send-label` is Cisco's equivalent to Huawei's `label-route-capability` for enabling MPLS label exchange in BGP\\n2. `disable-connected-check` serves a similar purpose to `check-tunnel-reachable` by allowing BGP sessions between non-directly connected peers when MPLS tunneling is used\\n\\nThe Cisco implementation doesn't have a direct 1:1 command for the tunnel reachability check, so we use these two commands to achieve similar functionality.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.3.1.1 disable-connected-check'}]]": 1,
